   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Planes: going to",
    "@en": "Plans: going to"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Para hablar de lo que piensas hacer se usa **to be + going to + verbo**: **I'm going to visit my parents** (voy a visitar a mis padres). Es igual que «ir a» en español.",
     "@en": "To talk about what you're going to do, **to be + going to + verbo**: **I'm going to visit my parents** is used (I'm going to visit my parents). It's just like «go to» in Spanish."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Negación: **I'm not going to work**. Pregunta: **What are you going to do?**",
     "@en": "Denial: **I'm not going to work**. Question: **What are you going to do?**"
    },
    {
     "@es": "Palabras de futuro: **tomorrow** (mañana), **tonight** (esta noche), **this weekend** (este fin de semana), **next week** (la semana que viene).",
     "@en": "Future words: **tomorrow** (tomorrow), **tonight** (tonight), **this weekend** (this weekend), **next week** (next week)."
    }
   ]
  },
